146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (The Simon Says FPGA Game is a memory-based digital game implemented using VHDL on an FPGA development board. Players must memorize and repeat LED sequences using push buttons, with the sequence becoming longer each level. The FPGA switches are used to select different game modes by controlling the LED delay speed, allowing players to choose from easier slow modes to more challenging fast modes.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
